{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'cat docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-trace-to-eval-sample.md; echo \"=====SUMS=====\"; cat docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/G03-SHA256SUMS; echo \"=====SPEC=====\"; cat harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-trace-to-eval-sample.md'","aggregated_output":"# G03：脱敏失败轨迹 → 可复跑评测样例\r\n\r\n日期：2026-10-13（Asia/Shanghai）。包码：G03（TF-0291）。真实 provider 调用：无。\r\n\r\n## 链路\r\n\r\n`scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.mjs`：\r\n\r\n- `traceToEvalSample(trace)`：把一条脱敏轨迹转成样例；`expected = { before-fix: fail|pass, after-fix: pass }`（failure 轨迹 before-fix=fail，其余保持 pass）。\r\n- `traceToEvalSamples(traces)`：显式触发批处理（仅调用方选定轨迹；可对应最近 7 天 runIds），逐条留 rejected 诊断。\r\n\r\n## 约束\r\n\r\n- **有界 reproducer**：`kind ∈ { scenario, route, command-id }`；不是 shell 指令。\r\n- **selector 可定位**：`{ runId, attempt }` 供 replay。\r\n- **确定性**：样例含 digest。\r\n- **脱敏闸门**：出现 `prompt/messages/body/authorization/apiKey/headers` 或 `sk-/phc_/ghp_/AKIA/私钥` 等即拒绝整条（`trace-not-redacted`），不写样例。\r\n- **显式触发**：不做定时 automation/daemon；不删原始证据。\r\n\r\n## 实测\r\n\r\n| 断言 | 结果 |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| failure 轨迹 → before-fix fail / after-fix pass；digest 确定 | ✅ |\r\n| success/refusal/cancelled → pass | ✅ |\r\n| raw prompt 或密钥 → 整条拒绝 | ✅ |\r\n| 非有界 reproducer（shell）→ 拒绝 | ✅ |\r\n| 批处理逐条留 rejected 诊断 | ✅ |\r\n| 缺字段 → 拒绝 | ✅ |\r\n\r\n## 残余（residual）\r\n\r\n- 本包提供转换器；把它接到具体 trace 存储/runner 属集成层。\r\n- 不新建 scenario registry/daemon/定时任务；不改默认值/锁/approval；非真人证据。\r\n=====SUMS=====\r\nb2936554a04cf2500ca099bb643a6345aadf451b0c77bcbe76428271c7452949  docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-acceptance.json\r\n0fe5f1fe54dbf41bf6a83c65d366cb55f7872d8f10f5ccfb3ce967399f30d757  docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-trace-to-eval-sample.md\r\nf0d8e2b9991d932ce267a9e88671357687f22f6b34d26f73366271185879aab7  harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-trace-to-eval-sample.md\r\nf67ed77b6202878d75bd5eb18661e8bf49fa791907edd1ed4889529b469ecc28  scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.mjs\r\na74711233bbd97060d9a8e16723c3b37b45f263e9b2b8987b82f63b53f4865f8  scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.d.mts\r\n9895c0c9296985a31e8c1beceac7d3a1d3c4918899f1d84a3ea3441ba38c4d70  tests/unit/trace-to-eval-sample.test.ts\r\n=====SPEC=====\r\n---\r\nlifecycleStatus: completed\r\nid: harness-gap-trace-to-eval-sample\r\ntitle: 把脱敏失败轨迹转成可复跑评测样例（G03）\r\nscenario: agent-dev-composable-scenarios\r\ntaskType: evaluation-harness\r\nintent: G03 提供一个显式触发的转换器：把选定的脱敏失败轨迹转成可复跑评测样例（before-fix=fail / after-fix=pass），样例绑定有界 reproducer 与 selector，并拒绝任何未脱敏（raw prompt / 密钥 / auth 头）的轨迹，防止泄漏。不做定时 automation / 后台 daemon。\r\ntouchedAreas:\r\n  - scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.mjs\r\n  - scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.d.mts\r\n  - tests/unit/trace-to-eval-sample.test.ts\r\n  - harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-trace-to-eval-sample.md\r\n  - docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-trace-to-eval-sample.md\r\n  - docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-acceptance.json\r\n  - docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/G03-SHA256SUMS\r\nownedPaths:\r\n  - scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.mjs\r\n  - scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.d.mts\r\n  - tests/unit/trace-to-eval-sample.test.ts\r\n  - harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-trace-to-eval-sample.md\r\n  - docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-trace-to-eval-sample.md\r\n  - docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-acceptance.json\r\n  - docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/G03-SHA256SUMS\r\nrequiredProfiles:\r\n  - fast\r\nrequiredRules:\r\n  - docs-sync\r\n  - task-forest-autoclose-and-roles\r\n  - repository-artifact-retention\r\nhumanEvidence: not-required\r\nrequiredTests:\r\n  - tests/unit/trace-to-eval-sample.test.ts\r\nacceptance:\r\n  - 一条真实失败轨迹 → 一个可复跑样例：before-fix 期望 fail、after-fix 期望 pass；成功/拒绝/取消轨迹保持 pass（修复不得回归）。\r\n  - 样例绑定有界 reproducer（kind ∈ scenario|route|command-id，非 shell）与 selector（runId+attempt），含确定性 digest 供 replay 对比。\r\n  - 拒绝未脱敏轨迹：出现 raw prompt/messages/body/authorization/apiKey/headers 或 sk-/phc_/ghp_/AKIA/私钥 等即整条拒绝，不写入样例（防泄漏）。\r\n  - 显式触发批处理：仅转换调用方选定的轨迹（可对应最近 7 天 runIds），每个被拒轨迹单独留诊断；不新建定时 automation / daemon。\r\n  - 不改产品默认值/锁/approval；不删除原始证据。\r\n  - 干净候选定向测试、类型、scoped lint、harness validate/dry-run 通过，凭据扫描 0 命中，SHA256SUMS 可回读。\r\nexpectedUserBehavior:\r\n  - 维护者能显式地把一条脱敏失败轨迹沉淀成可复跑评测样例（修复前 fail、修复后 pass），未脱敏轨迹被拒绝而非泄漏。\r\ndocs:\r\n  required: true\r\n  files:\r\n    - docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g03-trace-to-eval-sample.md\r\n---\r\n\r\n# G03 冻结实施边界\r\n\r\nG03 只新增一个纯转换器 + 显式触发的批处理入口（`scripts/lib/trace-to-eval-sample.mjs`），把选定脱敏轨迹转成可复跑样例；不做定时 automation/daemon，不新建第二份 scenario registry（样例指向既有 agent-dev scenario/route/command-id）。未脱敏轨迹整条拒绝。\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'cat openclaw_runtime/src/agents/sessions/extensions/shadow-write-event-recorder.ts; echo \"=====POLICY=====\"; cat openclaw_runtime/src/agents/sessions/extensions/policy-light-snapshotter.ts'","aggregated_output":"/**\r\n * A1 Layered Execution Isolation — Shadow write-event recorder (Stage 2 Stream 2C).\r\n *\r\n * Context: Round 2 design. During the \"shadow\" phase (before A1 is fully active),\r\n * we observe tool writes and check whether they match the declared\r\n * `writeRiskProfile.declaredWritePaths`. Writes to paths NOT in the declared set\r\n * are recorded as `undeclared_write_event` for later analysis.\r\n *\r\n * This is observe-only (shadow) — it does NOT block or modify writes. It only\r\n * records mismatches so we can measure declaration quality before promoting A1\r\n * to advisory/active modes.\r\n *\r\n * Acceptance criteria:\r\n * - 2.7: Shadow records `undeclared_write_event` when a tool writes to a path\r\n *   not in `declaredWritePaths`.\r\n * - 2.8: 0 `undeclared_write_event` when all tools declare correctly.\r\n *\r\n * See: docs/runtime-design/development-manual.md §Stage 2, Stream 2C\r\n *      docs/runtime-design/area-1-layered-execution-isolation.md §9.2\r\n */\r\n\r\nimport type { WriteRiskProfile } from \"../../../shared/tool-registration.js\";\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * A single undeclared write event — recorded when a tool writes to a path\r\n * that is not in its declared `writeRiskProfile.declaredWritePaths`.\r\n */\r\nexport type UndeclaredWriteEvent = {\r\n  /** Name of the tool that performed the write. */\r\n  toolName: string;\r\n  /** The path that was written to (was not declared). */\r\n  path: string;\r\n  /** The declared write paths for the tool (for context). */\r\n  declaredPaths: string[];\r\n  /** Timestamp of the event. */\r\n  timestamp: number;\r\n};\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Result of comparing actual writes against declared paths.\r\n */\r\nexport type UndeclaredWriteResult = {\r\n  /** Paths that were written but not declared. */\r\n  undeclaredPaths: string[];\r\n  /** Whether any undeclared writes were detected. */\r\n  hasUndeclared: boolean;\r\n};\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Pure function: detect undeclared writes by comparing actual write paths\r\n * against declared paths.\r\n *\r\n * Uses path-prefix matching: a write to `dir/file.txt` is considered declared\r\n * if `dir/file.txt` is in the declared set, OR if `dir/` is a declared prefix\r\n * (for `pattern_writes` / `declared_paths` that point to directories).\r\n *\r\n * @param declaredPaths Paths declared by the tool's `writeRiskProfile`.\r\n * @param actualPaths Paths actually written to during the turn.\r\n * @returns The set of undeclared paths.\r\n */\r\nexport function detectUndeclaredWrites(\r\n  declaredPaths: readonly string[],\r\n  actualPaths: readonly string[],\r\n): UndeclaredWriteResult {\r\n  const declaredSet = new Set(declaredPaths.map(normalizePath));\r\n  const undeclaredPaths: string[] = [];\r\n\r\n  for (const actualPath of actualPaths) {\r\n    const normalized = normalizePath(actualPath);\r\n    if (!isPathDeclared(normalized, declaredSet)) {\r\n      undeclaredPaths.push(actualPath);\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return {\r\n    undeclaredPaths,\r\n    hasUndeclared: undeclaredPaths.length > 0,\r\n  };\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Shadow write-event recorder — collects `undeclared_write_event` records\r\n * across one or more turns.\r\n *\r\n * Usage:\r\n * 1. Create with tool profiles (declared write paths per tool).\r\n * 2. After each turn, call `recordActualWrites(toolName, actualPaths)` with\r\n *    the paths that were actually written (from the snapshotter's fs-diff).\r\n * 3. Call `getEvents()` to retrieve all recorded events.\r\n * 4. Call `clear()` between sessions.\r\n */\r\nexport class ShadowWriteEventRecorder {\r\n  private events: UndeclaredWriteEvent[] = [];\r\n  private declaredPathsByTool: Map<string, string[]> = new Map();\r\n  private dynamicWriteTools: Set<string> = new Set();\r\n  private patternWriteTools: Set<string> = new Set();\r\n\r\n  constructor(toolProfiles: Array<{ name: string; profile: WriteRiskProfile }>) {\r\n    for (const { name, profile } of toolProfiles) {\r\n      if (profile.kind === \"declared_paths\") {\r\n        this.declaredPathsByTool.set(name, profile.writePaths.map(normalizePath));\r\n      } else if (profile.kind === \"pattern_writes\") {\r\n        // Pattern-matching tools use glob patterns (e.g., \"*.log\") that can't\r\n        // be verified by exact/path-prefix matching without a glob matcher.\r\n        // For shadow measurement, pattern_writes tools are NOT flagged —\r\n        // they declared their behavior, and verifying glob matches is out of\r\n        // scope for Stage 2 shadow measurement.\r\n        this.patternWriteTools.add(name);\r\n      } else if (profile.kind === \"dynamic_writes\") {\r\n        // dynamic_writes tools declare that they write to arbitrary paths.\r\n        // These are NOT flagged as undeclared — the tool explicitly declared\r\n        // that it uses dynamic_writes.\r\n        this.dynamicWriteTools.add(name);\r\n      }\r\n      // no_writes tools have no declared paths — any write is undeclared.\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  /**\r\n   * Record actual writes for a tool. If the tool wrote to paths not in its\r\n   * declared `writeRiskProfile`, `undeclared_write_event` records are created.\r\n   *\r\n   * - `dynamic_writes` tools: never flagged (they declared dynamic behavior).\r\n   * - `pattern_writes` tools: never flagged (glob matching out of scope).\r\n   * - `declared_paths` tools: writes outside declared paths are flagged.\r\n   * - `no_writes` tools: ANY write is flagged as undeclared.\r\n   *\r\n   * @param toolName Name of the tool.\r\n   * @param actualPaths Paths actually written to during the turn.\r\n   */\r\n  recordActualWrites(toolName: string, actualPaths: readonly string[]): void {\r\n    // dynamic_writes and pattern_writes tools are never flagged.\r\n    if (this.dynamicWriteTools.has(toolName) || this.patternWriteTools.has(toolName)) {\r\n      return;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    const declaredPaths = this.declaredPathsByTool.get(toolName) ?? [];\r\n    const { undeclaredPaths } = detectUndeclaredWrites(declaredPaths, actualPaths);\r\n\r\n    for (const path of undeclaredPaths) {\r\n      this.events.push({\r\n        toolName,\r\n        path,\r\n        declaredPaths,\r\n        timestamp: Date.now(),\r\n      });\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  /**\r\n   * Get all recorded `undeclared_write_event` records.\r\n   */\r\n  getEvents(): readonly UndeclaredWriteEvent[] {\r\n    return this.events;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  /**\r\n   * Get the count of recorded events.\r\n   */\r\n  getEventCount(): number {\r\n    return this.events.length;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  /**\r\n   * Check if any undeclared writes were recorded.\r\n   */\r\n  hasEvents(): boolean {\r\n    return this.events.length > 0;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  /**\r\n   * Clear all recorded events (e.g., between sessions).\r\n   */\r\n  clear(): void {\r\n    this.events = [];\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// Helpers\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Normalize a path for comparison: forward slashes, no trailing slash,\r\n * lowercase (for case-insensitive matching on Windows).\r\n */\r\nfunction normalizePath(p: string): string {\r\n  return p.replace(/\\\\/g, \"/\").replace(/\\/+$/, \"\").toLowerCase();\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Check if a (normalized) actual path is declared.\r\n *\r\n * A path is considered declared if:\r\n * - It exactly matches a declared path, OR\r\n * - A declared path is a prefix of it (directory match): e.g., declared\r\n *   `output/` covers `output/file.txt`.\r\n */\r\nfunction isPathDeclared(normalizedPath: string, declaredSet: Set<string>): boolean {\r\n  // Exact match.\r\n  if (declaredSet.has(normalizedPath)) {\r\n    return true;\r\n  }\r\n  // Prefix match: declared `dir/` covers `dir/file.txt`.\r\n  for (const declared of declaredSet) {\r\n    if (declared.endsWith(\"/\") && normalizedPath.startsWith(declared)) {\r\n      return true;\r\n    }\r\n    // Also handle the case where declared is `dir` (no trailing slash)\r\n    // and actual is `dir/file.txt`.\r\n    if (normalizedPath.startsWith(declared + \"/\")) {\r\n      return true;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  return false;\r\n}\r\n=====POLICY=====\r\n/**\r\n * A1 Layered Execution Isolation — PolicyLightSnapshotter (Stage 2 Stream 2A-3).\r\n *\r\n * Context: Round 2 design. Replaces A1's runtime path tracking with static\r\n * tool declarations. Snapshots `declaredWritePaths ∩ actual_fs_diff` and\r\n * integrates with A6 file fingerprints (single source of truth, §9.1).\r\n *\r\n * Modes:\r\n * - \"git-diff\": uses `git diff` against HEAD (or a baseline commit) to detect\r\n *   file changes. Behaviorally equivalent to today's snapshotter when A6 is off.\r\n * - \"copy-on-write\": copies declared write paths to a checkpoint directory\r\n *   before the turn; restores them on rollback.\r\n *\r\n * Integration:\r\n * - Reads fingerprints from A6 (`getFileFingerprint` / `fingerprintFromRecord`)\r\n *   READ-ONLY. Only A6 writes fingerprints.\r\n * - Git-diff fallback when A6 flag is off (acceptance 2.5, 2.6).\r\n * - For `dynamic_writes` tools, performs full fs-diff (acceptance 2.3).\r\n *\r\n * Flag-off parity (acceptance 2.11): when A1 flag is off, the snapshotter\r\n * returns a no-op handle — `begin()` / `commit()` / `rollback()` are no-ops.\r\n *\r\n * See: docs/runtime-design/development-manual.md §1.1 (A1), Stage 2 Stream 2A\r\n *      docs/runtime-design/area-1-layered-execution-isolation.md §9.1, §9.2\r\n */\r\n\r\nimport { execFile } from \"node:child_process\";\r\nimport { mkdir, copyFile, rm, stat } from \"node:fs/promises\";\r\nimport { join, dirname } from \"node:path\";\r\nimport { promisify } from \"node:util\";\r\n\r\nimport {\r\n  type DirectoryFingerprint,\r\n  type FileFingerprintDiff,\r\n  computeFileFingerprintsForDirectory,\r\n  diffFileFingerprints,\r\n  fingerprintFromRecord,\r\n} from \"../../long-task-control/file-fingerprint.js\";\r\nimport type { WriteRiskProfile } from \"../../../shared/tool-registration.js\";\r\n\r\nconst execFileAsync = promisify(execFile);\r\n\r\n/** Snapshot mode — determines how the diff is computed. */\r\nexport type SnapshotMode = \"git-diff\" | \"copy-on-write\";\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Plan for a snapshot — what mode to use and which paths to track.\r\n *\r\n * - When `dynamicWriteTools` is non-empty, falls back to full fs-diff\r\n *   (git-diff mode over the whole workspace).\r\n * - When `declaredWritePaths` is non-empty AND all tools declare paths,\r\n *   uses copy-on-write mode (only snapshots the declared paths).\r\n */\r\nexport type SnapshotPlan = {\r\n  mode: SnapshotMode;\r\n  /** Paths explicitly declared by write tools (from writeRiskProfile). */\r\n  declaredWritePaths: string[];\r\n  /** Tools with `dynamic_writes` profile (forces full fs-diff). */\r\n  dynamicWriteTools: string[];\r\n  /** Workspace root for resolving relative paths. */\r\n  workspaceRoot: string;\r\n  /** Whether A6 fingerprint integration is enabled (flag-gated). */\r\n  a6FingerprintEnabled: boolean;\r\n  /** Baseline fingerprint from A6 (when enabled, for copy-on-write mode). */\r\n  baselineFingerprint?: DirectoryFingerprint;\r\n};\r\n\r\n/** Handle to an active snapshot — supports commit / rollback / discard. */\r\nexport type SnapshotHandle = {\r\n  /** Unique ID for this snapshot. */\r\n  id: string;\r\n  /** The plan that produced this snapshot. */\r\n  plan: SnapshotPlan;\r\n  /** Timestamp when the snapshot was begun. */\r\n  begunAt: number;\r\n  /**\r\n   * Commit the snapshot — records the post-turn state and releases resources.\r\n   * Called after a successful turn.\r\n   */\r\n  commit: () => Promise<void>;\r\n  /**\r\n   * Rollback the snapshot — restores the pre-turn state.\r\n   * Called when the turn fails or is cancelled.\r\n   */\r\n  rollback: () => Promise<void>;\r\n  /**\r\n   * Discard the snapshot without committing or rolling back.\r\n   * Called when the snapshot is no longer needed (e.g., turn was a no-op).\r\n   */\r\n  discard: () => Promise<void>;\r\n  /** Diff computed after the turn (available after `commit`). */\r\n  diff?: FileFingerprintDiff;\r\n};\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Result of `beginSnapshot` — either a handle (success) or an error.\r\n */\r\nexport type SnapshotResult =\r\n  | { ok: true; handle: SnapshotHandle }\r\n  | { ok: false; reason: string; detail?: string };\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Configuration for the PolicyLightSnapshotter.\r\n */\r\nexport type PolicyLightSnapshotterConfig = {\r\n  /** Workspace root path (for git-diff and path resolution). */\r\n  workspaceRoot: string;\r\n  /** Whether A1 is enabled (flag-gated). Default: false (no-op). */\r\n  a1Enabled?: boolean;\r\n  /** Whether A6 fingerprint integration is enabled. Default: false (git-diff fallback). */\r\n  a6FingerprintEnabled?: boolean;\r\n  /** Baseline fingerprint record from A6 checkpoint (when enabled). */\r\n  baselineFingerprintRecord?: Record<string, string>;\r\n  /** Max files to snapshot in copy-on-write mode. Default: 1000. */\r\n  maxFilesForCopyOnWrite?: number;\r\n  /** Timeout for git commands in ms. Default: 5000. */\r\n  gitTimeoutMs?: number;\r\n};\r\n\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// Helpers\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * S1 fix (P1): Remove the snapshot directory with retry.\r\n *\r\n * Windows (and some network filesystems) may have a brief delay between a\r\n * file handle closing and the OS releasing the directory entry for deletion.\r\n * This helper retries the removal up to `maxRetries` times with a small\r\n * backoff, ensuring the snapshot directory is reliably cleaned up before\r\n * `commit()` / `rollback()` / `discard()` returns.\r\n */\r\nasync function removeSnapshotDirWithRetry(\r\n  snapshotDir: string,\r\n  maxRetries = 3,\r\n  backoffMs = 50,\r\n): Promise<void> {\r\n  for (let attempt = 0; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++) {\r\n    try {\r\n      await rm(snapshotDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\r\n      // Verify removal — if the directory no longer exists, we're done.\r\n      try {\r\n        await stat(snapshotDir);\r\n        // Directory still exists after rm — wait and retry.\r\n      } catch {\r\n        return; // ENOENT — successfully removed.\r\n      }\r\n    } catch {\r\n      // rm itself threw — wait and retry.\r\n    }\r\n    if (attempt < maxRetries) {\r\n      await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, backoffMs * (attempt + 1)));\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  // P2 fix: log when best-effort cleanup gives up after all retries, instead\r\n  // of silently swallowing the failure. The snapshot directory may leak on\r\n  // disk — this is not fatal (next session will overwrite) but should be\r\n  // observable for diagnostics.\r\n  try {\r\n    await stat(snapshotDir);\r\n    console.warn(\r\n      `[PolicyLightSnapshotter] failed to remove snapshot directory after ${maxRetries + 1} attempts: ${snapshotDir}`,\r\n    );\r\n  } catch {\r\n    // Directory was actually removed — no warning needed.\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Collect declared write paths from a set of tool write-risk profiles.\r\n * Returns the union of all `declared_paths` and `pattern_writes` patterns\r\n * (patterns are returned as-is for git-diff to interpret).\r\n */\r\nexport function collectDeclaredWritePaths(\r\n  toolProfiles: Array<{ name: string; profile: WriteRiskProfile }>,\r\n): { declaredPaths: string[]; dynamicTools: string[] } {\r\n  const declaredPaths: string[] = [];\r\n  const dynamicTools: string[] = [];\r\n\r\n  for (const { name, profile } of toolProfiles) {\r\n    if (profile.kind === \"declared_paths\") {\r\n      declaredPaths.push(...profile.writePaths);\r\n    } else if (profile.kind === \"pattern_writes\") {\r\n      // Patterns are added to the path list — git-diff will interpret them.\r\n      declaredPaths.push(profile.writePattern);\r\n    } else if (profile.kind === \"dynamic_writes\") {\r\n      dynamicTools.push(name);\r\n    }\r\n    // no_writes tools contribute nothing.\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return {\r\n    declaredPaths: [...new Set(declaredPaths)], // dedupe\r\n    dynamicTools,\r\n  };\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Execute a git command in the workspace root.\r\n */\r\nasync function git(\r\n  workspaceRoot: string,\r\n  args: string[],\r\n  timeoutMs: number,\r\n): Promise<{ stdout: string; stderr: string }> {\r\n  return execFileAsync(\"git\", args, {\r\n    cwd: workspaceRoot,\r\n    timeout: timeoutMs,\r\n    maxBuffer: 10 * 1024 * 1024, // 10 MB\r\n  });\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Get the set of changed files in the working tree.\r\n *\r\n * Uses `git ls-files --modified --others --exclude-standard` to detect both\r\n * modified tracked files AND untracked files (respecting .gitignore). This is\r\n * more comprehensive than `git diff --name-only HEAD`, which only shows tracked\r\n * file modifications and misses newly-created untracked files.\r\n *\r\n * Returns a list of changed file paths (relative to workspace root).\r\n */\r\nasync function gitDiffChangedFiles(\r\n  workspaceRoot: string,\r\n  timeoutMs: number,\r\n): Promise<string[]> {\r\n  try {\r\n    const { stdout } = await git(\r\n      workspaceRoot,\r\n      [\"ls-files\", \"--modified\", \"--others\", \"--exclude-standard\"],\r\n      timeoutMs,\r\n    );\r\n    return stdout.split(\"\\n\").filter(Boolean);\r\n  } catch {\r\n    // Not a git repo, or git unavailable — fall back to empty diff.\r\n    return [];\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// No-op handle (flag-off parity)\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nfunction createNoOpHandle(plan: SnapshotPlan): SnapshotHandle {\r\n  return {\r\n    id: `noop-${Date.now()}`,\r\n    plan,\r\n    begunAt: Date.now(),\r\n    commit: async () => {},\r\n    rollback: async () => {},\r\n    discard: async () => {},\r\n  };\r\n}\r\n\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// Copy-on-write snapshot\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nasync function beginCopyOnWriteSnapshot(\r\n  plan: SnapshotPlan,\r\n  _config: PolicyLightSnapshotterConfig,\r\n): Promise<SnapshotResult> {\r\n  const snapshotDir = join(\r\n    plan.workspaceRoot,\r\n    \".openclaw\",\r\n    \"snapshots\",\r\n    `snap-${Date.now()}`,\r\n  );\r\n\r\n  try {\r\n    await mkdir(snapshotDir, { recursive: true });\r\n  } catch (err) {\r\n    return {\r\n      ok: false,\r\n      reason: \"mkdir_failed\",\r\n      detail: String((err as Error).message),\r\n    };\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  // Copy the declared write paths to the snapshot directory.\r\n  const copiedPaths: string[] = [];\r\n  for (const relPath of plan.declaredWritePaths) {\r\n    const src = join(plan.workspaceRoot, relPath);\r\n    const dst = join(snapshotDir, relPath);\r\n    try {\r\n      const stats = await stat(src);\r\n      if (stats.isFile()) {\r\n        await mkdir(dirname(dst), { recursive: true });\r\n        await copyFile(src, dst);\r\n        copiedPaths.push(relPath);\r\n      }\r\n    } catch {\r\n      // File doesn't exist yet — it will be created during the turn.\r\n      // No need to snapshot a non-existent file.\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const handle: SnapshotHandle = {\r\n    id: `cow-${Date.now()}`,\r\n    plan,\r\n    begunAt: Date.now(),\r\n    commit: async () => {\r\n      // Compute diff if A6 fingerprint is available.\r\n      if (plan.a6FingerprintEnabled && plan.baselineFingerprint) {\r\n        const after = await computeFileFingerprintsForDirectory(plan.workspaceRoot, {\r\n          include: (relPath) => copiedPaths.includes(relPath),\r\n        });\r\n        handle.diff = diffFileFingerprints(plan.baselineFingerprint, after);\r\n      }\r\n      // S1 fix (P1): retry snapshot directory cleanup to handle Windows\r\n      // filesystem async delete delay. Retry up to 3 times with 50ms backoff.\r\n      await removeSnapshotDirWithRetry(snapshotDir);\r\n    },\r\n    rollback: async () => {\r\n      // Restore copied files from snapshot.\r\n      for (const relPath of copiedPaths) {\r\n        const src = join(snapshotDir, relPath);\r\n        const dst = join(plan.workspaceRoot, relPath);\r\n        try {\r\n          await copyFile(src, dst);\r\n        } catch {\r\n          // File may have been deleted during the turn — ignore.\r\n        }\r\n      }\r\n      await removeSnapshotDirWithRetry(snapshotDir);\r\n    },\r\n    discard: async () => {\r\n      await removeSnapshotDirWithRetry(snapshotDir);\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  return { ok: true, handle };\r\n}\r\n\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// Git-diff snapshot\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nasync function beginGitDiffSnapshot(\r\n  plan: SnapshotPlan,\r\n  config: PolicyLightSnapshotterConfig,\r\n): Promise<SnapshotResult> {\r\n  const timeoutMs = config.gitTimeoutMs ?? 5000;\r\n\r\n  // Record the pre-turn changed files (for diff computation).\r\n  const preTurnChanged = await gitDiffChangedFiles(plan.workspaceRoot, timeoutMs);\r\n\r\n  const handle: SnapshotHandle = {\r\n    id: `git-${Date.now()}`,\r\n    plan,\r\n    begunAt: Date.now(),\r\n    commit: async () => {\r\n      // Compute the post-turn changed files.\r\n      const postTurnChanged = await gitDiffChangedFiles(plan.workspaceRoot, timeoutMs);\r\n      // The diff is the set of files that changed DURING the turn.\r\n      const changedDuringTurn = postTurnChanged.filter(\r\n        (p) => !preTurnChanged.includes(p),\r\n      );\r\n      // Build a simple diff (we don't have full fingerprints here, but we\r\n      // record the changed files for diagnostics).\r\n      handle.diff = {\r\n        added: changedDuringTurn.map((p) => ({\r\n          path: p,\r\n          sha256: \"\",\r\n          mtimeMs: 0,\r\n          size: 0,\r\n        })),\r\n        removed: [],\r\n        modified: [],\r\n        touched: [],\r\n        summary: {\r\n          addedCount: changedDuringTurn.length,\r\n          removedCount: 0,\r\n          modifiedCount: 0,\r\n          touchedCount: 0,\r\n          isClean: changedDuringTurn.length === 0,\r\n        },\r\n      };\r\n    },\r\n    rollback: async () => {\r\n      // Git-diff rollback: restore changed files to HEAD.\r\n      try {\r\n        await git(plan.workspaceRoot, [\"checkout\", \"--\", ...preTurnChanged], timeoutMs);\r\n      } catch (err) {\r\n        // P2 fix: log the rollback failure instead of silently swallowing it.\r\n        // Git checkout may fail if files don't exist in HEAD — this is\r\n        // expected for newly-created files, but should be observable.\r\n        const message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err);\r\n        console.warn(\r\n          `[PolicyLightSnapshotter] git checkout rollback failed for ${preTurnChanged.length} files: ${message}`,\r\n        );\r\n      }\r\n    },\r\n    discard: async () => {\r\n      // No resources to release for git-diff mode.\r\n    },\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  return { ok: true, handle };\r\n}\r\n\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n// Main entry point\r\n// -------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Begin a snapshot for the current turn.\r\n *\r\n * - When A1 is disabled (flag-off parity), returns a no-op handle.\r\n * - When `dynamicWriteTools` is non-empty, uses git-diff mode (full fs-diff).\r\n * - When `declaredWritePaths` is non-empty AND no dynamic tools, uses\r\n *   copy-on-write mode.\r\n * - When A6 fingerprint is enabled, uses it as the baseline for diff.\r\n *\r\n * @param toolProfiles Write-risk profiles from registered tools.\r\n * @param config Snapshotter configuration.\r\n */\r\nexport async function beginSnapshot(\r\n  toolProfiles: Array<{ name: string; profile: WriteRiskProfile }>,\r\n  config: PolicyLightSnapshotterConfig,\r\n): Promise<SnapshotResult> {\r\n  const { declaredPaths, dynamicTools } = collectDeclaredWritePaths(toolProfiles);\r\n\r\n  // Load A6 baseline fingerprint if available.\r\n  let baselineFingerprint: DirectoryFingerprint | undefined;\r\n  if (config.a6FingerprintEnabled && config.baselineFingerprintRecord) {\r\n    baselineFingerprint = fingerprintFromRecord(\r\n      config.baselineFingerprintRecord,\r\n      config.workspaceRoot,\r\n    );\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  const plan: SnapshotPlan = {\r\n    mode: dynamicTools.length > 0 ? \"git-diff\" : \"copy-on-write\",\r\n    declaredWritePaths: declaredPaths,\r\n    dynamicWriteTools: dynamicTools,\r\n    workspaceRoot: config.workspaceRoot,\r\n    a6FingerprintEnabled: config.a6FingerprintEnabled ?? false,\r\n    baselineFingerprint,\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  // Flag-off parity: when A1 is disabled, return no-op handle.\r\n  if (!config.a1Enabled) {\r\n    return { ok: true, handle: createNoOpHandle(plan) };\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  // No write paths and no dynamic tools → no-op (nothing to snapshot).\r\n  if (declaredPaths.length === 0 && dynamicTools.length === 0) {\r\n    return { ok: true, handle: createNoOpHandle(plan) };\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  // dynamic_writes tools → full fs-diff (git-diff mode).\r\n  if (dynamicTools.length > 0) {\r\n    return beginGitDiffSnapshot(plan, config);\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  // Otherwise → copy-on-write mode (snapshots only declared paths).\r\n  const maxFiles = config.maxFilesForCopyOnWrite ?? 1000;\r\n  if (declaredPaths.length > maxFiles) {\r\n    // Too many files to copy — fall back to git-diff.\r\n    return beginGitDiffSnapshot({ ...plan, mode: \"git-diff\" }, config);\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return beginCopyOnWriteSnapshot(plan, config);\r\n}\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I understand the shape of the task. The task target scope is:\n\n1. `harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` — modify: add missing counter test to requiredTests and add coverage guard? The acceptance says \"spec drift: a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\" So the spec's requiredTests originally lacked the deprecation-counters test; we add `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` or `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts`. Wait, \"计数器测试原缺\" — the counter test (deprecation-counters) was originally missing from requiredTests. We add it, plus a coverage guard. And \"原门限字节不变\" means the original thresholds bytes unchanged — the graduation gate numbers stay identical.\n\n2. `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` — new test file mapping 4 graduation criteria to executable evidence.\n\n3. `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md` — new task spec.\n\n4. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md` — new doc.\n\n5. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json` — new acceptance.\n\n6. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS` — new sums.\n\nLet me look at the existing tests for reference (deprecation-counters test path) and understand what \"coverage guard\" means. Let me also look at whether some existing test references a required test path. Let me check `scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.mjs` and any test that validates requiredTests existence.\n\nLet me search for something that verifies requiredTests files exist / coverage guard patterns.\n\nLet me look at harness-gap baseline test and other \"coverage guard\" patterns."}}
