{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me look at how existing acceptance tests check \"requiredTests\" coverage, and at the source-inventory.json for A1 pilot contract. Also check what the task requires us to create:\n\nTarget scope:\n1. `harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` — modify: add the counter test to requiredTests with coverage guard, thresholds bytes unchanged.\n2. `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` — new test that maps the 4 graduation criteria to executable evidence, asserts legacy fallback rate <5% violated/not-violated, p99 budget, declaredPathViolationCount tracked, checkBudgetViolation('a1') degrade_to_legacy.\n3. `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md` — new spec (the \"harness-gap\" task spec).\n4. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md` — new doc.\n5. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json` — new acceptance record.\n6. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS` — checksums.\n\nNow let me understand the \"spec drift\" fix. The a1 spec's `requiredTests` currently lists:\n- tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts\n- tests/unit/policy-light-snapshotter.test.ts\n- tests/unit/shadow-write-event-recorder.test.ts\n- tests/unit/trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts\n- tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n\nNone of these files exist! The actual coverage is in `tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts` plus `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts`. So the task says \"a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\"\n\nHmm. \"原门限字节不变\" = \"original threshold bytes unchanged\" — i.e., don't change the graduation gate thresholds (5%, 200ms). Let's understand what needs to be done:\n- Add the counter test (`openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts`? or a new test) to requiredTests.\n- Add a coverage guard.\n\nLet me check `harness/src/rules.mjs` for requiredTests handling and whether there's a requiredTests existence check.\n\nLet me also check scripts/scan-pattern.mjs and the harness spec portability test.\n\nLet me read rules.mjs fully and the portability test."}}
