{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"cat docs/runtime-design/area-composition-spec.md | Select-String -Context 3 \\\"4\\\\.5|4\\\\.14|200ms|p99|graduation\\\" | Select-Object -First 60\"","aggregated_output":"\r\n  \r\n  **File**: `shared/types/evidence.ts` (created in Stage 0).\r\n  \r\n> ### Blocker 3: A3 graduation depends on A4, but A4 may be deprecated first\r\n  \r\n  **Problem**: A3's deprecation criteria states \"Mission reviewer 采信 anomalyPattern 后的决策质量（通过 A4 离线分析）\r\n不低于基线\". A4's deprecation criteria states \"90 天内被调用少于 3 次则启动废弃评估\". If no one runs A4, A4 gets deprec\r\nated, and A3 can never graduate.\r\n  \r\n> **Resolution**: **A3 graduation uses Mission decision outcome tracking, not A4.**\r\n  \r\n> A3's graduation metric changes from \"A4 offline analysis shows decision quality not below baseline\" to:\r\n  - \"In 100 consecutive Mission decisions where `anomalyPattern` was non-null, the decision was not downgraded (to `blo\r\ncked` or `sleep`) within the subsequent 5 ticks at a rate higher than the baseline (Mission decisions without anomalyPa\r\nttern).\"\r\n  \r\n> This uses existing `mission_runs` records (Mission Control's own outcome tracking), not A4. If A4 is deprecated, A3 g\r\nraduation is unaffected. A4 may still be used as an optional diagnostic tool during A3 review, but it is not a graduati\r\non dependency.\r\n  \r\n  ### Blocker 4: A1+A6 I/O during mid-turn pause\r\n  \r\n  \r\n  - Fixed size (current: `MAX_REPORTS = 200`).\r\n  - New kind registration requires `estimated_events_per_minute` estimate.\r\n> - If a new kind would cause ring overflow at p99, registration is rejected — must increase ring size or deprecate an \r\nold kind first.\r\n  - Kind count cap: 10 (enforced by `MAX_LCP_KINDS`).\r\n  \r\n  ### 5.3 SQLite write throughput\r\n  \r\n  ### 5.5 Per-turn cumulative latency budget\r\n  \r\n> - Cumulative p99 per turn: ≤ 300ms (A5 pre-turn 30ms + A1 post-turn 200ms + overhead).\r\n  - If exceeded: degrade by area priority — A4 (if it had any per-turn cost, it doesn't) → A3 → A5 → A1. A2 and A6 are \r\nnot per-turn and are not degraded by this rule.\r\n  \r\n  ### 5.6 Shadow total memory budget\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'cat harness/src/git.mjs'","aggregated_output":"import { execFile } from 'node:child_process';\r\nimport { promisify } from 'node:util';\r\nimport { ROOT } from './specs.mjs';\r\n\r\nconst execFileAsync = promisify(execFile);\r\n\r\nexport function resolveDiffBase(explicitSince, configuredDiffBase, defaultBase = 'origin/main') {\r\n  return explicitSince || configuredDiffBase || defaultBase;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * Default comparison base when neither `--since` nor the spec's `diffBase` is set.\r\n *\r\n * `origin/main` is the right base for a short-lived branch off the trunk, but this\r\n * repository develops on one long-lived integration branch: the diff against\r\n * `origin/main` is the whole branch divergence (thousands of files), so the\r\n * changed-path ownership gate failed for every task spec and the command was only\r\n * usable with `--no-diff`. The branch's own upstream is the base that means \"what\r\n * this branch has not pushed yet\". `origin/main` stays the fallback for a detached\r\n * HEAD or a checkout with no upstream, such as CI.\r\n */\r\nexport async function resolveDefaultDiffBase(cwd = ROOT) {\r\n  try {\r\n    const { stdout } = await execFileAsync(\r\n      'git',\r\n      ['rev-parse', '--abbrev-ref', '--symbolic-full-name', '@{upstream}'],\r\n      { cwd, encoding: 'utf8' },\r\n    );\r\n    const upstream = stdout.trim();\r\n    if (upstream && upstream !== '@{upstream}') return upstream;\r\n  } catch {\r\n    // No upstream configured: detached HEAD, CI checkout, or a purely local branch.\r\n  }\r\n  return 'origin/main';\r\n}\r\n\r\nasync function gitPaths(args, cwd = ROOT) {\r\n  const { stdout } = await execFileAsync('git', args, { cwd, encoding: 'utf8' });\r\n  return stdout.split('\\0').filter(Boolean);\r\n}\r\n\r\n// A base ref that does not resolve must fail closed. Swallowing the git error\r\n// and returning an empty file list would make every downstream changed-path\r\n// ownership check vacuously pass, which is the failure mode the RC-09\r\n// remediation plan (section 6) forbids.\r\nexport async function assertDiffBase(since, cwd = ROOT) {\r\n  const base = typeof since === 'string' ? since.trim() : '';\r\n  if (!base) throw new Error('diff base must be a non-empty ref');\r\n  try {\r\n    await execFileAsync('git', ['rev-parse', '--verify', `${base}^{commit}`], { cwd, encoding: 'utf8' });\r\n  } catch {\r\n    throw new Error(`invalid or missing diff base ref: ${base}`);\r\n  }\r\n  return base;\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport async function getChangedFiles(since = 'origin/main', cwd = ROOT) {\r\n  await assertDiffBase(since, cwd);\r\n  const files = new Set();\r\n  for (const file of await gitPaths(['diff', '--name-only', '-z', `${since}...HEAD`], cwd)) files.add(file);\r\n  for (const file of await gitPaths(['diff', '--cached', '--name-only', '-z'], cwd)) files.add(file);\r\n  for (const file of await gitPaths(['diff', '--name-only', '-z'], cwd)) files.add(file);\r\n  for (const file of await gitPaths(['ls-files', '--others', '--exclude-standard', '-z'], cwd)) files.add(file);\r\n  return [...files].sort();\r\n}\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I understand the structure. Let me plan the deliverables:\n\nTarget scope (files to create/modify):\n1. `harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` — modify: add the missing counter test to requiredTests, add a coverage guard, keep thresholds byte-identical (add `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` to requiredTests and coverage guard).\n2. `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` — new: maps 4 graduation criteria to executable evidence + guards spec drift.\n3. `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md` — new gap task spec.\n4. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md` — new closure doc.\n5. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json` — new acceptance record.\n6. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS` — new sums.\n\nThe task says: \"逐条把 4 个毕业判据映射到当前候选的可执行证据；不重定义门限；记录 spec requiredTests 缺口修正（计数器测试原缺）与残余。\"\n\nKey acceptance criteria:\n- 判据1 legacy fallback rate < 5%: deprecation-counters 单测断言 >5% → violated、<=5% → not violated（数值门限未改）。\n- 判据2 p99 ≤ 200ms: performance-budgets 断言 p99 预算。\n- 判据3 declaredPathViolationCount 单独计数并被跟踪。\n- 判据4 checkBudgetViolation('a1') 在 rate>5% 时返回 action=degrade_to_legacy。\n- 工具 writeRiskProfile 声明与命名空间拒绝（claw.a4.tool.choice on a1）由 tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement 覆盖。\n- 发现并修正 spec drift：a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\n- 干净候选定向测试、类型、scoped lint、harness validate/dry-run、comms replay/compare 通过，凭据扫描 0 命中，SHA256SUMS 可回读。\n\nSo the main implementation work:\n1. The a1 spec's `requiredTests` currently lists: tool-registration, policy-light-snapshotter, shadow-write-event-recorder, trace-namespace-enforcement, performance-budgets. It's MISSING the A1 deprecation counter test. Note the existing counter test in `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` is A5-only — it does NOT test A1. So there's a genuine gap: no test asserting A1 counter semantics (legacy fallback rate gate, declaredPathViolationCount separation, checkBudgetViolation('a1') degrade). This is the \"spec drift\" — the a1 spec requiredTests never included an A1 counter test, and the spec's acceptance references criteria 1, 3, 4 that had no executable evidence.\n\nAlso requiredTests references files that don't exist as `tests/unit/*`! Let me check: are there tests at `tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts`? No. What about `openclaw_runtime/src/...`? The requiredTests list points to `tests/unit/<name>.test.ts` — those don't exist. Hmm. Let me search whether those tests exist anywhere.\n\nLet me check for these files:\n- tool-registration.test.ts\n- policy-light-snapshotter.test.ts\n- shadow-write-event-recorder.test.ts\n- trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts\n- performance-budgets.test.ts\n\nEarlier checks: all False. Let me search wider.\n\nActually the deep tests (`tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts`) cover tool-registration, policy-light-snapshotter, shadow-write-event-recorder. And `tests/unit/observability-namespace.test.ts` covers namespace. So the spec's requiredTests are stale references.\n\nHmm, this is a \"spec drift\" situation. The task says: \"记录 spec requiredTests 缺口修正（计数器测试原缺）与残余\" — record the requiredTests gap correction (counter test originally missing) and residuals.\n\nSo the key correction: add the A1 counter coverage. The task acceptance says: \"发现并修正 spec drift：a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\"\n\nSo I should:\n- Create `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` that maps each of the 4 graduation criteria + tool/namespace criteria onto executable assertions, including the A1 counter assertions (criterion 1, 3, 4).\n- Add that new test to the a1 spec's requiredTests (and add a coverage guard that asserts the spec lists this test file).\n- Keep the graduation thresholds byte-identical.\n\nAlso create the gap task spec, closure doc, acceptance json, SHA256SUMS.\n\nLet me first verify that the A1 counter semantics actually work as claimed by running the code. But node_modules doesn't exist, so I can't run vitest. The instruction says \"run relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\". So I can run node scripts that don't need deps. vitest requires deps → can't run.\n\nBut I can run the harness CLI (pure node), and check-spec-lifecycle.mjs, and the deprecation counters directly via node (ESM import of .ts won't work directly though — it's TypeScript). Hmm. `deprecation-counters.ts` is TypeScript. Can't import directly with node.\n\nHowever, `harness/src/*.mjs` are plain JS. And scripts like `check-spec-lifecycle.mjs` are plain JS. I can run those with node.\n\nLet me check whether type-stripping works: Node 24 supports `--experimental-strip-types` for TS files. Node 24.22 supports type stripping natively (unflagged since 22.18/23). Actually Node 23+ enables type stripping by default. Node 22.18+ too. So `node openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.ts` might work but it's a module with exports only; import from a .mjs test... The import specifier would be `.js` not `.ts`. In the TS source, imports use `.js` extension resolving to `.ts` via bundler. Node's type stripping requires the actual file extension. So `import ... from \"./deprecation-counters.js\"` would fail since only `.ts` exists.\n\nSo running the A1 evidence through node directly is hard. Let me test quickly.\n\nActually, I could write a small verification script that reads and evaluates? Better: I can write the new test as a real vitest test (standard), but for \"checks I actually ran\", I should run what's runnable:\n- `node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec ... --no-diff`\n- `node harness/src/cli.mjs run --spec ... --dry-run`\n- `node scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.mjs`\n- Possibly a credential scan script.\n- SHA256SUMS verification.\n\nLet me check what check scripts exist and whether they need deps.\n\nLet me look at scripts directory listing.\n\nActually, let me first check if type stripping works, and try running a quick node check of the A1 counter logic by writing a temporary .mts/.ts script. Let's test.\n\nLet me also check for existing \"credential scan\" and SHA256 verification scripts."}}
