{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_93","type":"reasoning","text":"No vitest installed. So I can't run vitest. But I can run node scripts directly. Let me check what checks are runnable without installing deps: `node scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.mjs`, `node harness/src/cli.mjs validate`, etc.\n\nLet me understand the task fully. The task requires:\n1. `harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` — fix spec drift: add deprecation-counters test to requiredTests + coverage guard, original thresholds byte-identical.\n2. `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` — new test mapping the 4 graduation criteria to executable evidence.\n3. `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md` — new task spec.\n4. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md` — closure doc.\n5. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json` — acceptance record.\n6. `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS` — checksums.\n\nWait—but \"原门限字节不变\" (original thresholds byte-unchanged). The spec is currently `lifecycleStatus: archived`. Hmm. Let me re-read: \"发现并修正 spec drift：a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\"\n\nSo the requiredTests list must add `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` (the counter test). And the thresholds (the 5% / 200ms) bytes unchanged.\n\nLet me check the a1 spec's current requiredTests:\n```\nrequiredTests:\n  - tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/policy-light-snapshotter.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/shadow-write-event-recorder.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts\n  - tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n```\n\nNone of these files exist! Let me check. `tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts` → False. So the requiredTests point to non-existent files. Hmm, that's a big drift. But the acceptance criteria only mention the counter test missing. Let me re-read the acceptance criteria:\n\n- 判据1 legacy fallback rate < 5%：deprecation-counters 单测断言 >5% → violated、<=5% → not violated（数值门限未改）。\n- 判据2 p99 ≤ 200ms：performance-budgets 断言 p99 预算。\n- 判据3 declaredPathViolationCount 单独计数并被跟踪。\n- 判据4 checkBudgetViolation('a1') 在 rate>5% 时返回 action=degrade_to_legacy。\n- 工具 writeRiskProfile 声明与命名空间拒绝（claw.a4.tool.choice on a1）由 tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement 覆盖。\n- 发现并修正 spec drift：a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\n- 干净候选定向测试、类型、scoped lint、harness validate/dry-run、comms replay/compare 通过，凭据扫描 0 命中，SHA256SUMS 可回读。\n\nSo the treatment is: create `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` that verifies the 4 graduation criteria map to executable evidence in the current candidate, and corrects the spec drift by adding the missing counter test to requiredTests of the a1 spec, plus a coverage guard (a test that asserts the spec's requiredTests are actually present / cover the criteria).\n\nNote `tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts` exists and covers tool-registration, policy-light-snapshotter, shadow-write-event-recorder. But the spec's requiredTests reference `tests/unit/*.test.ts` paths that don't exist. Interesting. So the \"spec drift\" is that the a1 spec's requiredTests reference non-existent test paths (they were never created at those paths), and the counter test is missing.\n\nGiven the acceptance criterion specifically says \"requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变\" — so I should:\n- add the counter test path to requiredTests, and\n- add a coverage guard test asserting the spec's requiredTests exist and cover the 4 criteria.\n\nBut wait, the other 5 requiredTests paths don't exist either. Hmm. Let me actually check the deep tests to see if they match. `tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts` exists. Are there also `tool-registration.test.ts` anywhere? No. So the spec's requiredTests are stale paths.\n\nBut the task's targetScope is limited: only those 6 files. And the acceptance criteria mention \"tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement 覆盖\" which maps to real files: `openclaw_runtime/src/plugins/tool-descriptor-cache.test.ts`? Let's check. Actually there's `openclaw_runtime/src/plugins/tool-descriptor-cache.test.ts`. Hmm.\n\nLet me re-read criterion 5: \"工具 writeRiskProfile 声明与命名空间拒绝（claw.a4.tool.choice on a1）由 tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement 覆盖。\" This says: these are covered by tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement. So the reverify doc should map each of the criteria to the executable evidence. And the coverage test `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` should assert that mapping is real (the referenced evidence exists and asserts the thresholds).\n\nThis is a \"gate reverify\" task — the deliverable is mostly verification artifacts (test + docs + sums) rather than product code. Let me look at the deep test more carefully and see what modules exist to write a real coverage test.\n\nThe key deliverable: `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` that:\n- criterion 1: asserts deprecation-counters >5% → violated, <=5% → not violated (using the real modules)\n- criterion 2: asserts performance-budgets p99 budget\n- criterion 3: declaredPathViolationCount counted separately\n- criterion 4: checkBudgetViolation('a1') returns action=degrade_to_legacy when rate>5%\n- criterion 5: tool-registration writeRiskProfile + namespace rejection\n- criterion 6: spec drift guard — the a1 spec requiredTests must include the counter test, and thresholds bytes unchanged\n\n\"performance-budgets 断言 p99 预算\" — is there a performance-budgets module? Let me search.\n\nLet me look for where 200ms appears in code, and check existing tests.\n\nLet me search for \"isolation hot path\" or budget modules.\n\nLet me check the docs/enhancements/01-layered-execution-isolation.md and docs/runtime-design for p99 budget definitions and see if there's an existing module.\n\nAlso I should look at how \"deep\" tests relate — maybe there's a script that validates that spec requiredTests exist. Let me check `check-test-coverage-baseline.mjs` and `validate-test-gates.mjs`.\n\nLet me investigate more."}}
