{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_99","type":"reasoning","text":"No node_modules; so vitest isn't installed. The task says \"run relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\". So I need to run checks that don't need dependencies — e.g., `node scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.mjs`, `node harness/src/cli.mjs validate`, `node scripts/check-test-coverage-baseline.mjs`, credential scan, sha256sums verify. And I can run pure-node verification of the A1 gate coverage by importing the TS sources with Node 24 (which supports type stripping for .ts).\n\nActually Node 24 can run .ts directly (type stripping). Let me plan the deliverable.\n\nDeliverables per targetScope:\n1. `harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` — this is the existing spec. Task requires: fix spec drift (requiredTests missing counters test) and add coverage guard. Wait — but the target scope lists this file, plus a NEW file `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md`, plus `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json`, `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS`.\n\nAcceptance criteria list 7 items. Let me re-read:\n\n1. 判据1 legacy fallback rate < 5%: deprecation-counters 单测断言 >5% → violated、<=5% → not violated（数值门限未改）。\n2. 判据2 p99 ≤ 200ms：performance-budgets 断言 p99 预算。\n3. 判据3 declaredPathViolationCount 单独计数并被跟踪。\n4. 判据4 checkBudgetViolation('a1') 在 rate>5% 时返回 action=degrade_to_legacy。\n5. 工具 writeRiskProfile 声明与命名空间拒绝（claw.a4.tool.choice on a1）由 tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement 覆盖。\n6. 发现并修正 spec drift：a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\n7. 干净候选定向测试、类型、scoped lint、harness validate/dry-run、comms replay/compare 通过，凭据扫描 0 命中，SHA256SUMS 可回读。\n\nHmm. The spec `a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` currently has `lifecycleStatus: archived`, and its requiredTests list:\n- tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts\n- tests/unit/policy-light-snapshotter.test.ts\n- tests/unit/shadow-write-event-recorder.test.ts\n- tests/unit/trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts\n- tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n\nNone of those files exist! Actual coverage: `tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts`, `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts`, `tests/unit/observability-namespace.test.ts`. So the drift: requiredTests points to non-existent files and lacks the deprecation-counters test.\n\nSo the task: create the deliverables. What is the \"gate coverage\" test? `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` — should map the 4 graduation criteria to executable evidence, and include a coverage guard asserting the a1 spec's requiredTests lists the counter test (i.e. drift fix), and asserting the original gate thresholds are byte-unchanged.\n\nHmm, but I can't run vitest. Still, the task says \"run relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\". So I write the test and evidence, and run non-dependency checks.\n\nLet me think about what the \"original gate thresholds byte-unchanged\" means: The acceptance text of criteria 1-4 in the spec body (\"Graduation gate\"): rate < 5%, p99 ≤ 200ms, declaredPathViolationCount decreasing trend over 3 sessions, checkBudgetViolation returns degrade_to_legacy when rate > 5%. These must not be redefined. So the coverage guard should hash/compare the graduation-gate text.\n\nLet's design:\n\n### 1. `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts`\nA node-environment vitest test that:\n- Imports `deprecationCounters` from `../../openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.js`(actually .ts path like other tests use `.js`).\n- Criterion 1: rate > 5% → checkBudgetViolation('a1').violated true; rate <= 5% → not violated. Uses 100-turn session semantics: legacyFallbackCount/shadowSuccessCount summing to 100.\n- Criterion 2: p99 ≤ 200ms — needs a performance-budgets source. There is no `performance-budgets.ts`. Hmm. The spec requiredTests references `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts` which doesn't exist. Criterion 2 is \"p99 ≤ 200ms: performance-budgets 断言 p99 预算\".\n\nHmm, is there an actual A1 p99 budget assertion anywhere? Let me search for the A1 isolation hot path budget constant. Let me search for \"200\" near isolation/hot path.\n\nActually maybe I should create a `performance-budgets` module? That's a bigger scope. Let me check targetScope again: only these 6 files. So the coverage test must assert the p99 budget via... hmm. Since no performance-budgets module exists in target scope, the coverage test must assert the p99 budget measured/declared somewhere. Let me search more carefully for an existing A1 p99 budget declaration.\n\nLet me grep for \"200ms\" and \"p99\" in runtime design docs and see if some module encodes it.\n\nLet me check `docs/runtime-design/area-composition-spec.md` §5.5: \"Cumulative p99 per turn: ≤ 300ms (A5 pre-turn 30ms + A1 post-turn 200ms + overhead)\". So A1 post-turn budget is 200ms. Is there a constant? Let me grep for \"post-turn\" budget or \"A1\" budget constants.\n\nLet me search for numbers like 200 with names.\n\nLet me do targeted grep."}}
