{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me now look at how existing packets with \"harness-gap\" tasks describe the requiredTests gap and coverage guard. The TASK says targetScope includes:\n- harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md (modify requiredTests)\n- tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts (new test)\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md (new spec)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md (new doc)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json (new)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS (new)\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. criterion1 legacy fallback rate <5%: deprecation-counters unit test asserts >5% → violated, <=5% → not violated.\n2. criterion2 p99 ≤ 200ms: performance-budgets asserts p99 budget.\n3. criterion3 declaredPathViolationCount counted separately and tracked.\n4. criterion4 checkBudgetViolation('a1') returns action=degrade_to_legacy when rate>5%.\n5. tool writeRiskProfile declaration & namespace rejection covered by tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement.\n6. Discover and fix spec drift: a1 spec's requiredTests originally missing counter tests; add them with coverage guard, original thresholds byte-unchanged.\n7. Clean candidate focused tests, types, scoped lint, harness validate/dry-run, comms replay/compare pass; credential scan 0 hits; SHA256SUMS verifiable.\n\nImportant: The spec `a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` has `requiredTests` listing tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts etc. which DON'T EXIST. And there's `tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts` that covers the writeRiskProfile parts. So the \"spec drift\" is that requiredTests references nonexistent tests and misses the counter test.\n\nThe fix per acceptance criteria 1,2,3,4 is to create `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` that:\n- reads the a1 spec's requiredTests and asserts coverage (a coverage guard)\n- imports deprecationCounters and asserts: legacy fallback rate >5% → violated → degrade_to_legacy; <=5% → not violated. declaredPathViolationCount separately counted. p99 ≤ 200ms budget assertion.\n\nLet me check the design doc for what \"performance-budgets\" should be. Also I must not redefine thresholds.\n\nLet me look at the existing docs for A1 gate to base the doc on, and understand the p99 budget. Let me check docs/runtime-design/area-1-layered-execution-isolation.md.\n\nActually the targetScope list is the set of files to create/modify. Let me focus:\n\n1. Modify `harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md`: add the counter test to requiredTests + coverage guard, keep thresholds unchanged (must not change the \"e.g. <5%\" values). Wait — acceptance says \"原门限字节不变\" (original thresholds byte-unchanged). So we add `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` to requiredTests. Hmm, but \"已补入并加 coverage 守卫\" = \"already added and coverage guard added\". The coverage guard probably lives in the new test file: it verifies that the requiredTests of the a1 spec includes the counter test and that referenced test files exist.\n\nWait — but there's a subtlety: the a1 spec also lists nonexistent tests (tool-registration.test.ts etc.). Should we also fix those? The acceptance says \"a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫\" — the gap was that the counter test was missing; add it plus a coverage guard. It doesn't say to remove the other entries. But a coverage guard that asserts all requiredTests exist would fail because tool-registration.test.ts doesn't exist. Hmm.\n\nLet me re-read: \"发现并修正 spec drift：a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\"\n\nSo: the spec drift discovered is: a1 spec's requiredTests lacked the counter test. Fix: add it, and add a coverage guard. The thresholds (<5%, 200ms, etc.) stay byte-identical.\n\nThe \"coverage guard\" is likely in the new test file: it asserts that the A1 graduation criteria are covered by executable evidence — i.e., maps each of the 4 criteria to test assertions. And possibly asserts the a1 spec's requiredTests includes the coverage test and the counter test.\n\nHmm, but wait. Actually maybe the \"coverage guard\" should be a test that ensures requiredTests entries all exist on disk. But then the pre-existing bogus entries (tool-registration.test.ts) would fail. Let me check: are those paths real?\n\n`tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts` → doesn't exist. `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/sessions/tools/tool-definition-wrapper.ts`... The real coverage is `tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts`.\n\nHmm. So the a1 spec's requiredTests are all wrong? Let me double check by searching whole repo for these exact filenames.\n\nLet me verify."}}
