{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_122","type":"reasoning","text":"No existing A1 p99 budget module. The task says \"判据2 p99 ≤ 200ms：performance-budgets 断言 p99 预算.\" — meaning in the new test, criterion 2 maps to a performance-budgets assertion on the p99 budget. So the a01 gate coverage test should assert that the exported p99 budget for A1 is 200ms, and that the observed/measured p99 ≤ 200ms (or that the budget constant equals 200). It must not redefine the threshold.\n\nThe task's targetScope files:\n- harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md (modify: fix spec drift, add counter test to requiredTests + coverage guard)\n- tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts (new)\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md (new)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md (new)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json (new)\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS (new)\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n1. criterion1 legacy fallback rate < 5%: deprecation-counters unit test asserts >5% → violated, <=5% → not violated (numeric threshold unchanged).\n2. criterion2 p99 ≤ 200ms: performance-budgets asserts p99 budget.\n3. criterion3 declaredPathViolationCount counted separately and tracked.\n4. criterion4 checkBudgetViolation('a1') returns action=degrade_to_legacy when rate>5%.\n5. tool writeRiskProfile declaration and namespace rejection (claw.a4.tool.choice on a1) covered by tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement.\n6. Fix spec drift: a1 spec's requiredTests originally missing the counter test; add it and add coverage guard, original threshold bytes unchanged.\n7. clean candidate focused test, type, scoped lint, harness validate/dry-run, comms replay/compare pass, credential scan 0 hits, SHA256SUMS readable.\n\nSo the main deliverable is a new test file `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` that maps the 4 graduation criteria to executable evidence, plus spec drift fix (add `tests/unit/deprecation-counters