real hot-path work N times, compute p99, and assert ≤ 200ms with generous margin — measuring pure in-memory work in a loop should be far under 200ms p99, so not flaky.\n\nCriterion 3: `declaredPathViolationCount` separately counted/tracked — increment it and verify it's independent from legacyFallback/shadowSuccess, and that `getArea('a1')` reports it.\n\nCriterion 4: `checkBudgetViolation('a1')` rate>5% → action === 'degrade_to_legacy'.\n\nCriterion 5: `assertWriteRiskProfileForTool` + `validateEventNamespace('claw.a4.tool.choice','a1')` rejected. Also the 6 built-in tools declare writeRiskProfile — can I check that? Let me check the tool declarations in bash.ts/write.ts/edit.ts/apply-patch.ts/bash-tools.exec.ts/bash-tools.process.ts. That's the \"All 6 built-in tools declare writeRiskProfile + risk\" criterion. Let me verify these files export profiles.\n\nLet me check.\n\nNow the spec edit: add the counter test to requiredTests and a coverage guard. Currently requiredTests lists 5 files that don't exist... The acceptance says the \"计数器测试原缺\" — the counter test was missing. So add `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` (the coverage test) to requiredTests? Hmm, \"已补入并加 coverage 守卫\" — add it (the counter test) and add a coverage guard. The coverage guard is likely a test (the a01 coverage test) that asserts the spec's requiredTests contains the counter test.\n\nGiven ambiguity, the safest: in the a1 spec's requiredTests, add an entry for the deprecation-counters counter test path. Since requiredTests must be runnable from clean checkout, but the existing 5 are already non-existent... Actually maybe they're meant to be existing in the repo. Let me re-check with case-insensitive search for these filenames anywhere.\n\nWe already saw they don't exist. Hmm, that means the a1 pilot spec is drift-y: it references test files that don't exist. The drift fix: requiredTests \"原缺计数器测试\" → add the counter test file. I'll add `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` and `o