me look at how new specs are namespaced: `harness-gap-*` names. The task target says `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md`. Good.\n\nThe new spec's `scenario:` — for harness-gap packets, L01 used `gateway-backend-communication` with taskType `runtime-bridge` and requiredProfiles fast+comms. E01/G03 used `agent-dev-composable-scenarios` + `evaluation-harness` + fast. For A01 which touches runtime-bridge + comms? The acceptance mentions comms replay/compare. Hmm. The design says A01 is under V phase (integration/pilot). Let me check what scenario `agent-dev-composable-scenarios` requires (requiredProfiles) so validate passes.\n\nLet me check scenario specs for agent-dev-composable-scenarios and gateway-backend-communication.\n\nGiven criterion 7 requires comms replay/compare to pass, and A01 touches parts of comms? The original a1 spec uses scenario gateway-backend-communication with fast+comms. I'll follow that: new spec scenario=gateway-backend-communication, taskType=runtime-bridge, requiredProfiles fast+comms, requiredRules including backend-communication-boundary, comms-regression, docs-sync, task-forest-autoclose-and-roles, repository-artifact-retention.\n\nBut wait: if scenario is gateway-backend-communication, validate enforces that touchedAreas cover changed files, and the backend boundary scan runs over changed + touchedAreas files that start with `src/`. My changes are in tests/, harness/, docs/ — none start with `src/`, so boundary scan is fine.\n\nAlso `validateChangedPathOwnership` requires every changed file matched by touchedAreas/ownedPaths. So I must list all changed files in both touchedAreas and ownedPaths. Let me include:\n- tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts\n- harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md\n- harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json\n- docs/dev/harness-gap-closure