{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"reasoning","text":"All 6 built-in tools declare writeRiskProfile. Now I understand the scope. The task is:\n\n1. Re-verify A1 layered isolation controlled pilot gate\n2. Map 4 graduation criteria to executable evidence in the current candidate\n3. Don't redefine thresholds\n4. Record spec drift correction (requiredTests originally missing counter test) and residuals.\n\nDeliverables in targetScope:\n- `harness/specs/tasks/a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` — the spec, needs updating requiredTests to add counter test + coverage guard\n- `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` — new test that verifies the 4 criteria against the current candidate\n- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md` — new task spec\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md` — closure doc\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json` — acceptance record\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS` — hashes\n\nLet me look at the current spec's requiredTests again. It lists:\n- tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts\n- tests/unit/policy-light-snapshotter.test.ts\n- tests/unit/shadow-write-event-recorder.test.ts\n- tests/unit/trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts\n- tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\n\nNone of these exist! The actual tests are `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` (A5 only) and `tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts`. So there's drift: requiredTests reference non-existent files, and there's no A1 counter test at all.\n\nThe acceptance criteria says:\n- 判据1: deprecation-counters unit test asserts >5% → violated, <=5% → not violated (threshold unchanged)\n- 判据2: performance-budgets asserts p99 budget\n- 判据3: declaredPathViolationCount counted separately and tracked\n- 判据4: checkBudgetViolation('a1') returns action=degrade_to_legacy when rate>5%\n- writeRiskProfile declaration and namespace rejection covered by tool-registration / trace-namespace-enforcement\n- spec drift: a1 spec requiredTests originally missing counter test; add it and add coverage guard, original thresholds byte-unchanged\n- clean candidate targeted tests, types, scoped lint, harness validate/dry-run, comms replay/compare pass, credential scan 0 hits, SHA256SUMS readable\n\nSo I need to write `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` that:\n1. Verifies criterion 1: counter test asserting rate >5% → violated and <=5% → not violated, using actual deprecationCounters\n2. Verifies criterion 2: performance budget p99 ≤ 200ms — this should be a measured budget assertion\n3. Verifies criterion 3: declaredPathViolationCount separate\n4. Verifies criterion 4: checkBudgetViolation('a1') returns degrade_to_legacy\n5. Verifies writeRiskProfile for all 6 built-ins + namespace rejection of claw.a4.tool.choice on a1\n6. A coverage guard that asserts the a1 spec's requiredTests now include the counter test and all required tests exist on disk (spec drift guard)\n\nLet me look at the deep test and the a4-deep test to understand namespace enforcement (the `claw.a4.tool.choice` on a1 rejection). Let me check trace-recorder.\n\nAlso, I need to understand: the spec `a1-layered-isolation-pilot.md` currently has `lifecycleStatus: archived`. The drift correction should add the counter test to requiredTests. Let me consider whether to change lifecycleStatus. The task says \"发现并修正 spec drift：a1 spec 的 requiredTests 原缺计数器测试；已补入并加 coverage 守卫，原门限字节不变。\" — so add counter test to requiredTests, keep thresholds unchanged. It says \"原门限字节不变\" meaning the acceptance thresholds text stays byte-identical.\n\nLet me look at trace-recorder.ts to see how namespace rejection is enforced there (claw.a4.tool.choice on a1).\n\nAlso let me check the deprecation-counters test file — it's A5 only. So a new counter test for A1 is genuinely missing.\n\nLet me read trace-recorder.ts."}}
