evidence:\n- `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` (new: the 4-criteria reverify coverage incl. counter assertions)\n- `tests/unit/deep/a1-deep.test.ts` (existing: tool-registration / policy-light-snapshotter / shadow-write-event-recorder)\n- `tests/unit/observability-namespace.test.ts` (existing: trace namespace enforcement)\n- `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` (existing: counter registry)\n\nand keep the original fictional entries? No — keeping non-existent entries makes the coverage guard fail. But removing them changes the gate list bytes. Hmm, \"原门限字节不变\" — I now think \"门限\" = thresholds/limits = the acceptance criteria numbers. The requiredTests list is not a \"门限\". And criterion 6 explicitly says the requiredTests gets fixed. So editing requiredTests is expected.\n\nHmm, but the safest minimal edit consistent with \"原缺计数器测试\": just add one line for the counter test, leaving the other five. Then the coverage guard should NOT require all entries to exist (since four are legacy placeholders), only that the counter test is present and that it (and the guard) exist. Hmm, but that leaves known-broken entries.\n\nUgh. Let me look for a \"spec-drift\" or \"coverage guard\" precedent in the repo to infer convention. Let me grep for tests that read spec requiredTests.\n\nLet me do that now.\n\nAlso check: is there a script that verifies requiredTests paths exist? Let me grep for \"requiredTests\" in scripts — check-repository-artifacts.mjs and agent-engineering-acceptance.mjs reference it.\n\nLet me look at those."}}
