\n(c) create `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-a1-isolation-gate.md`\n(d) create `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a01-acceptance.json`\n(e) create `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/A01-SHA256SUMS`\n(f) create `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a01-isolation-pilot-reverify.md` (the packet spec, contextRef)\n\nThe guard test likely checks the packet spec exists with required fields (like other packets' guard tests) and that the a1 spec's requiredTests now includes the counter test and thresholds unchanged, plus that the 5 required tests + counter test exist.\n\nLet me look at how other similar \"gate coverage\" guard tests are written for A02..A06 in the reference (they're hidden too, in `base`? No—`tests/unit/a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts` is in hiddenTestPaths, and likely not in base). Let me check whether base has them: earlier `base:False` for a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts, and for the others? Let me check base for a02-a06 coverage tests — if they exist in base, they'd be a template! Actually they're listed in hiddenTestPaths (a02..a06) but that's for their own tasks. Let me check if they exist anywhere in this workspace or base.\n\nLet me search."}}
