rkspace here is the agent workspace (post-scrub, pre-agent-work). Let me check what's actually in the workspace: `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts` exists (A5-only describe block per summary). And tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts doesn't exist (it's a preexisting guard path, scrubbed).\n\nSo the agent must:\n1. Create the source support needed so the restored oracle tests pass:\n   - `durable_state` WriteRiskProfile in tool-registration.ts\n   - `cross-area-facades.ts`\n2. Ensure `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts` (restored by grader) — wait, that's a preexisting guard path that the grader restores. The agent doesn't need to create it. But the a01 coverage test reads it (`read(\"tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts\")`). Since grader restores it, it will exist at grade time. Good.\n\n   Also `tests/unit/tool-registration.test.ts` is restored by grader → so the a01 coverage test's read of it works.\n   \n3. Create `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` — this is the hidden signal path; grader keeps its own copy and overwrites?? Actually \"hiddenSignalPaths\" — the grader has a hidden copy that it uses for grading. The agent must create it? The diff in trial-1 showed `diff.added: []` etc. Hmm, actually the trial-1 agent produced... let me look at what the agent's diff was. Actually historical-result.json showed diff added/changed/removed all empty — because the agent was killed / no git. Hmm, \"noGitMetadataAtStart\": true.\n\nActually the manifest says the deliverable list in TASK.json targetScope includes tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts. And the grader runs it. Since grader owns a hidden copy at hiddenSignalPaths, the grader presumably overwrites the agent's version with its own... or maybe the grader only removes preexisting oracle paths and keeps the agent's hidden signal file. Given \"hiddenTestsHiddenFromAgent\": true and the oracle ran the agent's file? In trial-1, the a01 coverage test failed asserting