{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_377","type":"reasoning","text":"So the grader tree has the original oracle `tool-registration.test.ts` (which requires `durable_state`), but the grade source `tool-registration.ts` in the grader tree is the base version (0 durable_state). The agent must supply `openclaw_runtime/src/shared/tool-registration.ts` (with durable_state) and `cross-area-facades.ts` in the agent workspace. The grader overlays the oracle test files from `preexistingGuardPaths` into the agent's tree, then runs.\n\nWait — actually, the grader's copy has tool-registration.ts too. Let me look more carefully — the grade layering: the grader dir contains full checkout. Then oracle test files (preexistingGuardPaths + hiddenSignalPaths) are restored from grader over the agent workspace. So everything else comes from the agent workspace.\n\nHmm, but the grader dir contains a tool-registration.ts with 0 durable_state. That's likely just the pristine base checkout. The runtime uses the agent's workspace copy of source files.\n\nSo the agent must:\n1. Add `durable_state` support to `openclaw_runtime/src/shared/tool-registration.ts`.\n2. Create `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts`.\n3. Fix the a1 spec.\n4. Write the coverage test, spec, docs, acceptance, SHA256SUMS.\n\nNote the manifest's targetScope doesn't list the source files, but acceptance criteria and the oracle require them. The referenceSolution only touched 4 files (docs/spec/coverage test) — but that's the *historical* reference commit which was based on a repo where cross-area-facades.ts and durable_state already existed. In our base commit (72ba3c3), they were removed. So the agent needs to restore them.\n\nHmm wait, but that's odd: the base commit is 72ba3c32e31cf071aa98c3ed335f76d9b12ef1c1, and the reference commit is 46e553fd87 with parent e619b6613. And base 72ba3c3 has tool-registration with 0 durable_state. So indeed the harness deliberately scrubbed these out of the