\tmp\\_a01_verify\\` as a directory whose `node_modules` is a junction to `D:\\ClawX\\node_modules`, and copy the agent workspace tree into it. The workspace tree size — let me check. Actually the agent workspace is a fresh git-archive (no node_modules), so copying it should be feasible.\n\nBut wait: vitest config resolution — `vitest.config.ts` uses workspace/project configs. Running `pnpm exec vitest run <7 files> --maxWorkers=1` from that dir should work if node_modules resolves.\n\nLet me check whether D:\\ClawX\\node_modules has vitest binary and whether junction across drives works (D: junction is fine on Windows).\n\nLet me first check sizes and set up.\n\nActually, there may be an even simpler approach: run vitest from within the agent workspace directory using `D:\\ClawX\\node_modules\\.bin\\vitest.cmd`, but node resolution for imports (vite, vitest packages) would fail because there's no node_modules in the agent dir or its parents... unless Node walks up: D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\trials\\tf-0293-a01-treatment-3\\agent → ... no node_modules anywhere up to D:\\ root. So no.\n\nThe junction approach is the way. Let me plan:\n1. Create `D:\\tmp\\_a01_verify\\` \n2. Copy the agent workspace (excluding .rsi? keep it, harmless) into it.\n3. `New-Item -ItemType Junction -Path D:\\tmp\\_a01_verify\\node_modules -Target D:\\ClawX\\node_modules`\n4. Run `D:\\ClawX\\node_modules\\.bin\\vitest.cmd run <files> --maxWorkers=1` with cwd = D:\\tmp\\_a01_verify.\n\nHmm, but pnpm workspaces: `openclaw_runtime/packages/agent-core` may be a pnpm workspace package with its own node_modules symlinks. Let me check whether `pnpm-lock.yaml` / `pnpm-workspace.yaml` includes them and whether D:\\ClawX\\node_modules is a pnpm store-based layout (yes, .pnpm). Then `openclaw_runtime/node_modules` might exist in D:\\ClawX. Let me check.\n\nAlso `vitest.config.ts` may have aliases. Let me read it.\n\nLet me first do reconnaissance on the verify setup and on what the tests import.\n\nAls