a/cross-area-facades.ts`.\n5. `tests/unit/trace-namespace-enforcement.test.ts`, policy-light-snapshotter, shadow-write-event-recorder → unchanged, should pass.\n\nBut wait — if the grader's copies are the CANDIDATE versions, then the whole \"candidate\" tree already has those source files. Why would the agent need to add durable_state?\n\nBecause the agent's workspace = BASE tree (72ba3c32), which lacks durable_state and cross-area-facades. The RSI harness's \"held-out\" oracle is the candidate revision's *test* files. The intent: the base tree's tests are the \"before\" state; the candidate's tests are the \"after\" state. These self-contained tasks are meant to be *reconstructible*: the agent reconstructs what the historical commit did, and the hidden tests verify.\n\nHmm, but that contradicts: the historical commit 46e553fd did NOT add durable_state or cross-area-facades. Those came from *other* commits between base and candidate.\n\nHmm. Let me check: is `durable_state` and `cross-area-facades` present in the BASE tree used by t1/t3? t3 base has `tool-registration.ts` = 7217cc1e (no durable_state), no cross-area. And t3 agent workspace: tool-registration.ts = 7217cc1e (no durable_state). So neither has it.\n\nSo the oracle test `tool-registration.test.ts` (candidate version, needs durable_state) is fundamentally INCONSISTENT with the base tree. That's why both prior trials failed with `failureClass=agent`.\n\nHmm... unless. The oracle is designed such that the agent must produce the delta. But the task description says \"Re-verify A1 layered-isolation controlled pilot gate\" — nothing about durable_state.\n\nWait. Maybe I'm misreading the base/candidate relationship. Let me check: is the t3 `base` dir really 72ba3c32? The manifest says source.candidate.commit = 96afc2c75..., and task baseCommit = 72ba3c32. And `isolation: \"fresh git-archive directory per trial\"`.\n\nHmm, \"fresh git-archive directory per trial\" — so the trial workspace = git archive of the CANDIDATE tree (96afc2c), then \"scrubbed\" (oracle paths removed). Let me verify: does the t3 base dir contain cross-area-facades.ts? Earlier: `openclaw_runtime\\src\\agents\\cross-area\\cross-area-facades.ts => False` in base. And t3 base package.json = ? Let me check if t3 base matches 96afc2c or 72ba3c32.\n\nThat's the crux! Let me check t3 base's package.json and orchestration-protocol.ts hashes.\n\nIf t3 base == 96afc2c tree, then t3 base's tool-registration.test.ts would be the candidate version with durable_state — but I measured t1 base's as 81781f18 (base version). Hmm, but that was t1. Let me measure t3's base.\n\nLet me do that now. This is the decisive check."}}
