requiredCapabilities, attemptPolicy, status. Let me check the base OrchestrationTaskGraph type to ensure the facades compile (TS) — though vitest doesn't typecheck by default (esbuild strips types). So type mismatches won't fail the test at runtime. Good. But `ContextBudgetPlanner` constructor calls `new ResourceAwareWaveScheduler(graph, {maxWorkers})` and `plan()` → `buildExecutionWaves(graph, maxWorkers)`. Need that to not throw. It exists in base. Good.\n\n`planner.replanOnResume(...)` → scheduler.getWaves().find(w=>w.status===\"planned\") etc. Should work.\n\n`verifier.verify({config: undefined}, bool)` → runRuntimeResumeShadow({config: undefined}) → resolveRuntimeEventLogFeatureFlags(undefined).resumeReplayShadow — likely false by default → disabled → enabled:false → requiresReverification = rollbackOccurred && enabled = false. Test expects `requiresReverification` to be false. ✓ (for cycle%2===0 → true&&false=false). ✓\n\n`coordinator.coordinatePause(...)` → leaseBeforeCheckpoint: lease.committedAt <= checkpoint.writtenAt → same `now` → true ✓.\n\n`planner.resumeReexecutions` must be 10 after 10 replanOnResume calls. replanOnResume: computes firstPlanned wave, calls rePlan({appliesToWave, maxWorkers: resumedMaxWorkers}). For it to be accepted, maxWorkers must differ from current. Test calls `planner.replanOnResume(3 - (cycle % 3))` → values 3,2,1,3,2,1,... and initial plan used maxWorkers=4. First call resumedMaxWorkers=3 ≠ 4 → accepted, currentMaxWorkers=3. Next cycle: 2 ≠ 3 → accepted. Then 1. Then 3 ≠ 1 → accepted. etc. Each accepted → resumeCount++ → 10. ✓ But careful: rePlan requires the target wave to exist and be \"planned\". After plan(), waves are planned. appliesToWave = first planned wave = 1. rePlan on wave 1: status planned → ok. newMaxWorkers differs → accepted. Then waves recomputed. Still planned. So each call accepted. ✓\n\nAlso `expect(contract.requiresReverification).toBe(false)` ✓.\n\nGood — the candidate's cross-area-facades should pass. S