pnpm install... no. I can run vitest directly: `node D:\\ClawX\\node_modules\\vitest\\vitest.mjs run ...` or use the `.bin` shim. Actually invoking `D:\\ClawX\\node_modules\\.bin\\vitest.cmd` from the scratch cwd — vitest resolves `process.cwd()`. Hmm, `.bin/vitest.cmd` runs node with the vitest CLI; the cwd would be the scratch dir. That should work.\n\nActually there's a subtlety: vitest resolves `vitest/config` and plugins (`@vitejs/plugin-react`) from the config file's location → it needs node_modules reachable from `D:\\tmp\\rsi-ver-a01`. With the junction, yes.\n\nLet me also confirm `@vitejs/plugin-react` is in ClawX node_modules. It's a devDependency; should be.\n\nLet me start implementing. First, clean up scratch files.\n\nLet me first check the OrchestrationTaskGraph type in base to be safe.\n\nLet me proceed step by step.\n\nLet me begin by removing the leftover probe files and creating the ports."}}
