h are now imported at exact candidate bytes.\n\nNow let me verify by running the oracle locally. I need a node_modules. Let me set up a run directory.\n\nImportant: the oracle runs `pnpm exec vitest run ... tests/unit/...` from the workspace root. It needs node_modules. Since I must not install dependencies, I can create a junction/symlink of node_modules into a copy of the workspace, then run vitest from D:\\ClawX\\node_modules\\.bin\\vitest.cmd.\n\nActually, the simplest: create a scratch directory at D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\_verify\\ (outside the trial dir), copy the workspace there, link node_modules, and copy the grader's restored tests in.\n\nBut copying 212MB is fine.\n\nActually even simpler: I can copy the workspace to a temp dir, then junction node_modules from ClawX. Let me do that. Then copy the 6 restored oracle tests (from grader) + my a01 coverage test + the modified a1 spec into place, and run the oracle command.\n\nLet's be careful: the grader's restored tests correspond to the candidate revision, which equals D:\\ClawX current worktree files for those 6 tests (verified hashes match: tool-registration 8690822b, perf-budgets 585be3c6, etc.). Actually let me verify: D:\\ClawX\\tests\\unit\\performance-budgets.test.ts was a27fb409... no wait.\n\nEarlier: `D:\\ClawX\\tests\\unit\\performance-budgets.test.ts` hash = 585be3c6a23b2023965e97e238535284e9e3a95d2752535a0e7e3875fa5d3635 — that's the candidate version. And grader = 585be3c6a23b... same. Good. And tool-registration: ClawX = 8690822b..., grader = 8690822b... same. Good.\n\nSo I can source the restored oracle tests directly from D:\\ClawX\\tests\\unit\\.\n\nHmm, but wait: D:\\ClawX is at commit cf06c348... (HEAD, much later than candidate 96afc2c). Yet its tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts hash equals the candidate blob. Interesting but fine — could be unchanged since candidate. Let me just verify precisely all 6 test files in D:\\ClawX match grader hashes. Earlier I verified: grader hashes = ClawX worktree hashes for performance-budgets (585be3c6) and tool-registration (8690822b) and a01-coverage (23b311a2). Let me check the others quickly too.\n\nLet me set up the verification run.\n\nActually, there's a subtlety: the workspace `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/orchestration-protocol.ts` differs (base 1585fc5a vs cand d5314886). The performance-budgets test only needs `OrchestrationTaskGraph` type (compile-time) and the cross-area-facades module. The cross-area-facades only imports types from orchestration-protocol, so base version is fine.\n\nBut: performance-budgets.test.ts imports `OrchestrationTaskGraph` and creates a graph object with `mode: \"auto\"`, `status: \"planned\"`. Need to check base OrchestrationGraphMode includes \"auto\". Let me check. Actually vitest/esbuild strips types, so type mismatches won't fail at runtime. The graph literal is fine regardless.\n\nAlso `ResourceAwareWaveScheduler` uses `buildExecutionWaves`. That exists in base. Good.\n\nLet me now set up the verification environment.\n\nPlan:\n1. Create D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\_verify\\ws — copy of the agent workspace (after my edits).\n2. Junction node_modules → C:\\Users\\27933\\.codex\\worktrees\\tf0604-rsi-baseline\\ClawX\\node_modules\n3. Copy the 6 restored oracle tests from D:\\ClawX\\tests\\unit\\ (grader versions).\n4. Run the oracle command.\n\nActually copying the whole workspace is ~212MB and 17.5k files. Fine.\n\nHmm, but I could avoid the copy: the workspace has no node_modules. vitest resolves node_modules by walking up parent dirs. If I place the workspace's parent (D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\trials\\tf-0293-a01-treatment-3\\) ... no, that would pollute the trial dir.\n\nBetter: create the junction directly inside the agent workspace? That would add a `node_modules` to the deliverable workspace — bad, and the grader diff would see it. Actually the trial snapshot/grader uses git-archive-like isolation... but `agentWrites`/diff detection could pick up node_modules.