\<trial>\\grader. Going up 5 levels from grader/tests/unit/... hmm.\n\nActually the cleanest approach: create the verification tree at D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\_a01verify\\ClawX (a sibling-like name), and inside it copy the workspace tree and junction node_modules → the baseline ClawX node_modules. Then nested junctions.\n\nLet me check: does pnpm exec work without pnpm-workspace? It should just find vitest in node_modules/.bin.\n\nLet me do it. Copy 212MB — acceptable.\n\nActually, I could avoid the copy by using directory junctions for the entire subtrees and only overlaying changed files. But overlaying is complex. A full copy is simplest and ~212MB.\n\nLet me do the copy with robocopy (fast, and I'll keep it inside the run dir where it's clearly scratch).\n\nActually, let me reconsider: is running the oracle locally even necessary? The task says \"run relevant existing checks that do not install dependencies\" and \"Report exact checks you actually ran.\" I should genuinely run the oracle-equivalent test command. That's the strongest evidence.\n\nLet me set it up.\n\nPlan:\n1. `D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\_a01verify\\ClawX` = copy of agent workspace.\n2. Junction `node_modules` → `C:\\Users\\27933\\.codex\\worktrees\\tf0604-rsi-baseline\\ClawX\\node_modules`.\n3. Junction nested ones: `openclaw_runtime\\node_modules`, `openclaw_runtime\\packages\\*\\node_modules`, `packages\\versebrowser\\node_modules`, `resources\\verseshell-mcp\\node_modules`.\n4. Copy the 7 grader test files into `tests/unit/`.\n5. Run `node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run <7 files> --maxWorkers=1`.\n\nWait, the pnpm `.bin/vitest.cmd` uses relative paths from its own dir. If I junction node_modules, `node_modules\\.bin\\vitest.cmd` will resolve `%~dp0\\..\\.pnpm\\...`. With a junction, `%~dp0` is the junction path, and `\\..\\.pnpm\\` exists in the target. But node_modules/.pnpm would be... let me check if node_modules/.pnpm exists as a symlink target. Actually the `.pnpm` dir is inside the